Objet: [unmarked] Seasonal p-values in ColExt MB GOF Test
Date: 2024-12-09 19:31:03

Hello all,

I am running a Mackenzie-Bailey Goodness of Fit test (using AICcmodavg)
on a dynamic occupancy model fit with colext. The model has 12 seasons
fit, but one season was entirely unsampled. Normally when running
mb.gof.test, the object returned has a list of p-values specific to
each season from the model, but the output of these GOF tests with a
missing season only returns a list of length one (instead or 12 or
perhaps 11 as one might expect). Is this an expected behaviour? Is
there a way to calculate the season-specific p-values when there is a
missing season?

Thanks,
Rory

